A||N||5||stimpy||Baby Steps||||1||
Z||000000||stimpy||06-25-2000||06:18 PM||||With all of the (well intentioned) talk here of organizing an international Fiero gathering, it seems that there is plenty of theoretical support for get-togethers. Anyone who has been around the forum any length of time can see that there is a very active cell of folks in the Ohio-Indiana area, and Golden Gate Fieros is a club that is very well represented in the forum.<P>What I persoally would love to see is some interest in gathering a group of folks in the south/southwest who would be intereted in participating in a fall meet in either Oklahoma City or Dallas. With all the enthusiasm that is on display here, I would think that at least 20 participants could be gathered. What do ya think, Dan3.8gt, 80's boy, pollock, WhiteFieroBlur... If I am leaving anyone out, let me know! I know Texans are down, how about Colorado, Kansas, Missouri<BR>and Arkansas? Any enthusiasm to take the hill before we go chaging up the mountain?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Majik||06-25-2000||09:00 PM||||Whatever you plan for the plains/mountains area, count me in.  I'm in the middle of organizing the New Mexico Fiero Association, and I'll bring who I can from the area!  <BR>I'll also have my ride pretty well finished by the end of summer/beginning of fall, so would be a good time to bring it and show it off.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Keep in touch with me if you need anything at all!<P>Todd<BR>Albuquerque, New Mexico<BR>86 GT||||reg||14
Z||000002||pollock||06-26-2000||01:42 PM||||Ohio's a long damn drive from here, stimp.....<P>I've gotta get some (read: a helluva lotta) work done on mine before i take it to any shows.  It's embarrassing to even drive it around.  <P>Think i'll install the Ttops first, at least get a minimal cool factor going on.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||06-26-2000||02:14 PM||||what about a couple get togethers, simultaneously around the us, and then find people in the local areas with fast internet services (i.e. dsl, cable, perhaps a sponsor at a business with a T1) and use microsoft netmeeting to use a kind of videoconference? its not gonna be everyone together at the same time, but it might be preferable for some people who do not want to travel too far. if anyone needs info on videoconferencing, contact me, i set up a system for the vista unified school district as a pilot for board meetings across the state.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||06-26-2000||02:28 PM||||<BR>Another South Texas Texan here.<P>I can't fathom the idea of driving to OH HI OH for a great big bash.  The guys in other states, unless they have lived in Tejas, appear to have no concept of distance.  When it takes 2 whole days to cross from (East to West) the state of Texas, that is pretty freaking big.<P>But, providing my Fiero does break on me, I would love to partcipate in something in and around the Dallas area. I would even go to Oklahoma, but as for going to Florida, California, or Ohio, forget it, it is just too cotton-pickin' far.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||06-27-2000||11:18 AM||||  Man Stimpy, as long as you and I have been Buds, I thought you would have remembered your kin here in Nevada. I might be interested in a southwest regional meet. I live in Vegas so Texas or Oklahoma would be cool. And I do mean cool, or at least cooler. Whew, It's hotter thatn hell here. Let me know what you come up with and I'll try and fit it in.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <P>  Late BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||8
